=over

=item April 16, 2018

The first one-liner uploaded to GitHub Gists as L<rename.pl|https://gist.github.com/justinnamilee/5f3d757beb3f63ba863b0877b790128c>.

 opendir(my $d, '.'); my @d = grep { -f } readdir($d); \
 print @d . qq( files found:\n); foreach my $o (@d) {  \
 if ($o =~ /x(\d\d)\s+-\s+(.+)/) { my $n =             \
 sprintf(qq(S09E%02d-E%02d %s), $1*2 -1, $1*2, $2);    \
 print qq($o\n\t$n\n); rename($o, $n) or warn $!; } }

=item May 6, 2024

The script moves into L<fairu-chan|https://github.com/justinnamilee/fairu-chan/commit/6d8aab629910ba0400596705860d36075e64c0fd>.

=item July 13, 2026

A L<new repository|https://github.com/justinnamilee/xmrf> dedicated to the tool is started.

=back

